"Among the top\u202f10 occupations in U.S.\u202fNews & World\u202fReport\u2019s 2025 \u201c100\u202fBest Jobs in America\u201d list, the only ones that earned a Future\u202fProspects score above\u202f9 were:\n\n| Rank | Occupation | Future\u202fProspects score | Median annual salary (U.S.\u202fNews 2024 data) |\n|------|------------|------------------------|-------------------------------------------|\n| 1 | Nurse\u202fPractitioner | **9.9** | **$129,210** |\n| 10 | Actuary | **9.3** | **$166,950** |\n\nBecause the Actuary\u2019s median salary ($166,950) is substantially higher than the Nurse\u202fPractitioner\u2019s ($129,210), **the Actuary is the profession with the highest median salary among those with a Future\u202fProspects rating exceeding\u202f9**."